{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"When powers have the same base, $\\dfrac{x^m}{x^n}=x^{m-n}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's apply that rule to our equation, $\\dfrac{4^{\\blueD{6}}}{4^\\greenD{x}}=4^\\goldD{0}$.\n\nWe can solve for $\\greenD{x}$ with the equation, $\\blueD{6}-\\greenD{x} = \\goldD0$.\n\n$\\begin{align} \\blueD{6}-\\greenD{x}\u0026= \\goldD0 \\\\\n\\greenD{x} \u0026= 6 \\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$x = 6$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Solve for $x$.**\n\n$\\dfrac{4^{6}}{4^x}=4^0$\n\n$x=$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":6}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"","size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
